# Client components (React 19 + Ant Design 6)

## File layout

One folder per component: `Name.jsx`, `Name.css`, `index.js`.

```js
// components/Loader/index.js
export { default } from './Loader'
```

- PascalCase folder and file names. Default export from `Name.jsx`, re-export from `index.js`.
- Shared components go in `client/src/components/`. Components used by exactly one page go in `pages/<area>/<Page>/components/`.
- Function components only. The project uses no PropTypes — do not add them to individual files.

## Imports

Use the `@/` alias inside `pages/` and `components/`. Use relative paths inside `hooks/`, `api/`, and `context/`, matching the surrounding files.

```jsx
import { useAppContext } from '@/context/AppContext'
import { IMAGE, RICH_TEXT } from '@/constants/ui'
```

## Styling

In order of preference:

1. Ant Design components and `theme.useToken()` values for spacing, color, radius, and font size.
2. Named constants from `@/constants/ui.js` for layout sizes, table widths, page size, date formats.
3. A co-located `.css` file for anything the above cannot express.

```jsx
const { token } = theme.useToken()
<Tag style={{ marginBottom: token.marginSM }}>{blog.category}</Tag>
```

Never hardcode a hex color or pixel spacing value that a token or `ui.js` constant already covers. CSS files are global, not modules, so prefix every class with the component name (`blog-card-title`, not `title`).

## Routes

Routes are declared only in `App.jsx`. Every path and path builder lives in `@/constants/routes.js`.

Do not hardcode a path in `navigate()` or `<Link>`. `Login.jsx` currently navigates to `'/register'` and `'/reset-password'`, which are missing from `ROUTES` — add them there rather than copying that pattern.

## Forms

Ant Design `Form` with `Form.useForm()` and declarative `rules`. Do not introduce react-hook-form or Formik. Validation messages use i18n keys under `validation.*`.

## Strings

User-facing text goes through `useTranslation()` and `client/src/i18n/locales/en.json`.

`@/constants/messages.js` is legacy and only still referenced by older hooks. Do not add new keys to it.

## Before finishing

- No `console.log` or `console.error` left in the code. `hooks/api/mutations/useCreateBlog.js` still has debug logging; do not copy that pattern.
- Run `npm run lint` in `client/`.
